<title>UK: Freddie Mac sets $500 million five-year bond, call.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac sets $500 million five-year bond, call.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager J.P. Morgan Securities.</p>
<p> BORROWER   FEDERAL HOME LOAN MORTGAGE CORP</p>
<p> AMT	  $500 MLN  COUPON     7.256     MATURITY   *17.SEP.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    17.SEP.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.25	REOFFER    PAR	 SPREAD	+55 BP</p>
<p> NOTES     *CALLABLE AT PAR AFTER TWO YEARS.</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  0.05	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.50 PCT U.S. TREASURY NOTE DUE 31.AUG.01 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
